      "message": "I just got an even better suggestion from Yi. We could be using \"-target aarch64-linux-android -march\u003darmv8.2a -mcpu\u003dgeneric -mtune\u003dcortex-a55\". -mtune will get us the cortex-a55 scheduling, but not any optional instructions. Using just armv8.2a as the -march gives us the minimal instruction set (without dotprod - actually there\u0027s a bug too where nodotprod does the wrong thing, but I\u0027ll get that addressed). The generic CPU is there in case the defaults change.\n\nCould you change the flags here to:\n\n...\n\"-march\u003darmv8.2a\",\n\"-mcpu\u003dgeneric\",\n\"-mtune\u003dcortex-a55\",\n...\n?\n\nI think that would be the optimal path forward, and also gives us the same code we are currently generating actually.",
